@endpoint = http://localhost:3000/api/matches


### Get all matches
GET http://localhost:3000/api/matches
Content-Type: application/json

### Create a new match
POST http://localhost:3000/api/matches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "home_team_id": "T001",
  "away_team_id": "T002",
  "score": 0,
  "date": "2024-12-01T15:00:00Z"
}

### Get a specific match by ID (replace with actual ObjectId from create response)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/matches/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
Content-Type: application/json

### Update a match by ID (replace with actual ObjectId)
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/matches/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "home_team_id": "T001",
  "away_team_id": "T002",
  "score": 1,
  "date": "2024-12-01T15:00:00Z"
}

### Delete a match by ID (replace with actual ObjectId)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/matches/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ===== ERROR SCENARIO TESTS =====

### 2. POST request which fails validation - Missing required fields
POST http://localhost:3000/api/matches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "home_team_id": "T001"
}

###

### POST request which fails validation - Invalid team references
POST http://localhost:3000/api/matches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "home_team_id": "InvalidTeam",
  "away_team_id": "T002",
  "score": 0,
  "date": "2024-12-01T15:00:00Z"
}

###

### POST request which fails validation - Same home and away team
POST http://localhost:3000/api/matches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "home_team_id": "T001",
  "away_team_id": "T001",
  "score": 0,
  "date": "2024-12-01T15:00:00Z"
}

###

### POST request which fails validation - Invalid date format
POST http://localhost:3000/api/matches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "home_team_id": "T001",
  "away_team_id": "T002",
  "score": 0,
  "date": "invalid-date"
}

###

